  "attribution": {
    "registration_gap": "The plain growth schedule permanently spent its one PnP trial before later registrations exposed stronger 2D-3D support. The bounded post-refinement pass recovered 6/7 baseline misses at cap64 and 9/9 misses at cap96.",
    "accuracy_gap": "The cap64 mapper stream discarded too much geometric support. Raising the cap to 96 reduced growth-only RMSE by 71.8%; iterative refinement then removed the remaining isolated pose error. Cap128 and uncapped growth were both worse, so more correspondences are not monotonically better with the current union-find conflict policy.",
    "selected_policy": "Electro uses an explicit cap96 plus the existing bounded post-refinement registration pass. The cap remains opt-in and is not a repository-wide default.",
    "stop_reason": "Cap128 and uncapped were two consecutive quality regressions after cap96; no higher-cap final refinement was run."
  },
